# Model fitting

- Every publication fit is driven by a committed configuration.
- Record the data checksum, animal IDs, feature order, parameter grids,
  optimizer settings, random seed, split identities, package version, and
  output paths.
- Preserve submitted behavior before refactoring it, including optimizer
  initialization and feature ordering.
- Each fit supports a one-animal smoke mode and a full publication mode.
- Write stable Parquet/JSON summaries; never make notebooks depend on `dill`.
- Refuse to overwrite an existing artifact with different provenance unless
  the caller explicitly requests replacement.
- Compare regenerated outputs with the committed golden summaries.
- Use exact checks for categorical/provenance values and documented numerical
  tolerances for floating-point values.
- Full model sweeps are release checks, not routine CI tests.
